 "result_text": "I fixed the MQTT publish so `$ext` functions in `json` are evaluated. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a broker.\n\nYour diagnosis was right. `update_from_ext` ran after `json` had already been turned into a string, so there was no dict left to find `$ext` in. Switching the key to `payload` wouldn't have helped either, for the same reason.\n\nIn `tavern/_plugins/mqtt/request.py`, `get_publish_args` now calls `update_from_ext(fspec, [\"json\"])` before `json.dumps`. I removed the old call that ran afterwards in `MQTTRequest.__init__`. Your request should work as written. The function's return value is merged into the `json` body alongside `thing_1: abc`, and the merged result becomes the payload.\n\nI didn't touch `payload:` given as a plain string. `$ext` only applies under `json:`.",
